# Netlify rewrite rules — not a redirect to a new URL, a rewrite that
# serves different content while keeping the URL the visitor sees.
#
# /templates renders content built to templates-page/index.html rather
# than templates/index.html, because templates/ is reserved for the
# site's page-template sources (raw files containing {{tokens}}, not
# meant to be a real page) and already sits at the repo root alongside
# every other output directory.
/templates              /templates-page/index.html   200
/templates/              /templates-page/index.html   200

# Everything else under /templates/* (templates/home.html, etc.) is a raw
# page-template source — {{tokens}} unresolved, never meant to be public.
# It was reachable because Netlify's pretty-URL resolution matches
# /templates/home straight to the literal file templates/home.html, which
# sits in the published root like every other file. Block it explicitly;
# the two exact-path rules above still take priority for the real page.
/templates/*             /index.html                  404
